{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_289","type":"agent_message","text":"Both exhaustive floor-tour matrices are negative: 42,940 movement steps cover every cell of every portal and physical component under all static phases. That leaves a transport/activation sequence, not a hidden floor trigger. I’m comparing level 6’s panel symbols with level 5’s known solved assembly to identify which icon is a destination versus a control—especially the missing magenta/blue `(13,8)` endpoint."}}
